module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.the_labs_only_model_route_is_a_hand_placed_tunnel_to_a_single_rented_card

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data the_labs_only_model_route_is_a_hand_placed_tunnel_to_a_single_rented_card: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "the_labs_only_model_route_is_a_hand_placed_tunnel_to_a_single_rented_card" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: every harness worker of the dev lab had one model route, an ssh -L tunnel started by a hand-placed systemd --user unit on srv1 (127.0.0.1:18090) to one card the operator rented (ssh1.vast.ai:32062, ninfer-serve, model id qwen). When the operator's rental ended (2026-10-17 03:28Z) the tunnel failed and the route was an unreachable address no model declared: the lab had no inference at all, and nothing in the repository said what replaced it. A route that is an address, a unit and a rental none of which the repository models is a single point of failure that is invisible until it fails.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a consumer whose only path to a model is a literal host:port plus a process the repository does not start. Ask what happens to the consumer when that one party stops, and who is told. The tell in the code is a route fact derived from a tunnel's LISTENER (harness_operator_route operator_endpoint_origin read operator_endpoint_tunnel.listener) rather than from a modeled upstream: the address a request is sent to cannot disagree with a forward nobody observed.",

    "REPAIRED at the interface/realization/policy split (DESIGN section 3): the pool front is its own upstream interface (extdeps.pool.pool_front, cited to the pool operator's ctrl #2375/#2376), the lab's choice to use it is policy (harness_operator_route harness_operator_route), and the pinned HTTPS client is the realization (http.Client PostJsonFromFileWithHeaderFilePinned). The tunnel row, the /health probe and the old card's model id are DELETED, not left as a second path. A front that cannot serve answers 503, 502 or 429, and a post may also draw no response at all: each means NOTHING WAS SERVED and no effect was taken, so the request is PATIENT (operator direction 2026-10-27, the patient request contract) -- the worker records ONE durable turn.request_pending event and exits, sleeping beside nothing and retrying nothing in-process; the belt re-delivers the SAME round of the SAME session when the re-delivery schedule (harness_transport_retry_policy: first delay doubling to a cap plus a session offset) says the next re-delivery is due, Holds naming that instant until then, and NOTHING EVER ENDS THE WAIT -- no budget, no expiry, no clock on a delivered request. A re-delivery is not a resume and never spends session_resume_bound; the /models wake probe is deleted (the re-delivery is the probe). A 401, a refused certificate, any other 4xx, or an unreadable response stays a terminal refusal. The discriminating claims are test.claim.operator_endpoint_witness: request shape (bearer, x-pool-session, model id), a different certificate refused before any request, 503/502/429 and a no-response post each yielding the one pending event with no in-process retry while 401 and 500 do not, and the real client's argv inhabiting the supplied shape; and test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_continuation_witness: due yields Resume of the same attempt_key, not-due yields Hold naming the next instant, ten days pending still yields only Resume or Hold, and re-pending keeps the window's opening.",

    "HARM: DESIGN section 5 externalized availability, silent until the card went. A lab with one hand-placed route cannot be qualified, resumed or moved, and the first signal was every worker failing at once. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the roster probe declined the route as unreachable). ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the route fact (it derives from a modeled upstream); the front's own availability is outside the modeled guarantee and is observed at the boundary. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the pool front's TLS card landing (fierce-swift-120 ctrl #2376) changes the live answer from 503 to a served turn; the lab qualification on srv1 is the first live reading of every figure in the extdeps module."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.pool.pool_front", decl_name: "pool_front_contract_standing", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.harness.harness_operator_route", decl_name: "harness_operator_route", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.harness.harness_turn", decl_name: "harness_post_json_once", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.operator_endpoint_witness", decl_name: "a_request_on_the_pool_route_carries_the_bearer_the_session_and_the_model", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
